{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'segment-matches|segment-key|B6|R5|dao.stream|dao.jing|register|stack|client|DHT|local|completion|Standalone|standalone|milestone|file box|Existing edits|one unit|together' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# yin.vm de Bruijn linker over dao.stream (Phase B6)\n8:`dao.stream` (backed by `dao.jing` content addressing). It is Phase B6 of\n11:Governing rule: **B6 is used by both the stack VM and the register VM for\n12:linking code over `dao.stream`.**\n14:Foundational principle: **The linker fetches code over `dao.stream`, but the\n15:code itself is stored in `dao.jing`.**\n18:AST, multiple execution backends (stack VM and register VM), peer witnesses\n20:`dao.jing`, while linking, resolution, and fetching occur strictly over\n21:append-only `dao.stream` boundaries. Upstream stages -- Yang, the resolver\n22:(B2), the stack lowerer (B2), and the register compiler (R1, R2) -- produce\n25:- Register images, identified by R (`:yin.debruijn.register`)\n28:verify, and link those executable images over `dao.stream`. A host holding\n35:Phase B6 is implemented alone as the dedicated linker phase. It establishes\n37:provides the concrete format records for both the stack and register VMs.\n39:## 2. Invariants: storage in dao.jing, fetching over dao.stream\n43:1. **Storage in `dao.jing`**: The executable code itself (the canonical\n44:   instruction vector or register image map) is stored as an immutable,\n45:   content-addressed value in `dao.jing`, located at its `segment-key`.\n46:2. **Fetching over `dao.stream`**: Linking is an append-only stream process.\n49:   `dao.stream`. No direct function calls cross process or host boundaries.\n51:   - `dao.jing.dht` handles local cache retrieval and Kademlia peer lookup.\n52:   - `dao.jing.remote` handles DHT requests over `dao.stream` using\n53:     `content-client` and `default-handlers`.\n55:B6 reu