{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-23 19:23:50 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 02:23:50 +0700 ICT\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\nThe two Round 1 findings are resolved. Step 2 now uses `jing/segment-matches?`, which reads the algorithm from the address. Section 11 also separates linker checks of corrupt local content and client responses from DHT peer filtering, which can yield `:absent`.\n\n- **P1 | [linker design:208](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md:208):** Both format records name `image-free-names` functions in existing code namespaces, but neither function exists. The [B6 file box](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md:316) permits only the new linker source and test files. Define the scanners in the new linker namespace and reference them there, or explicitly allow the required edits to the existing namespaces.\n- **P2 | [linker design:316](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md:316):** This document makes B6 the sole milestone and module for both formats, but the [register design’s R5 box](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1011) still requires a separate register linker source and test file. Reconcile that phase box so implementers have one deliverable contract.\n\nThe owner’s shared-linker and Jing-storage/DaoStream-transfer rules are clearly stated and architecturally sound in this document. B6 is bounded here to `debruijn_linker.cljc` and its test file; the two findings above prevent sign-off on that boundary. No files were edited."}}
